  "summary_en": "Vermont statute restricting law enforcement drone use. It bans drone use for investigating or prosecuting crime except with a warrant or recognized exception, limits data collection to the surveillance target, bars facial recognition on non-targets, and makes unlawfully gathered evidence inadmissible.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Law enforcement may not use drones to investigate, detect or prosecute crime except under subsection (c).",
   "Drones may not gather data on people exercising free speech and assembly rights.",
   "Permitted uses include search and rescue, disaster assessment, and warrant-based or exigent-circumstance use.",
   "Exigent use requires a warrant within 48 hours; if denied, use stops and data is destroyed.",
   "Facial recognition on non-targets is barred; evidence gathered in violation is inadmissible."
  ],
